PAGE npc7554 branch0 page0 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Hello, may I see your
proof of registration?
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page1 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Okay, now
you're ready to go.
In my class, I teach the
use of the most basic
interfaces.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page2 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Novice.
would you like to learn
more about interface
fundamentals?
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page3 mode5 choices3 text<>
 CHOICE 0 ordinal1 <Yes.>
 CHOICE 1 ordinal2 <Nah, I'm a pro~>
 CHOICE 2 ordinal3 <Cancel.>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page4 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Press Select to choose a window with the D-pad or left stick. Press A to open it, then A to enter its list. B returns. Highlight an open window and move it with the right stick; L3 restores its position. R3 closes the highlighted window.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page5 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Now, let me explain each interface window according to their default positions on your screen.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page6 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
At the upper left side of your screen, you will see a window with your character name and level. This is the ^3355FFBasic Information Window^000000.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page7 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Let me give you
some experience points.
Keep an eye on your Basic Info Window and observe the change in your Base Level experience gauge.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page8 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Did you see...?
As you gain experience,
the experience gauge fills up.
Once it is 100 % full, you gain an experience level, and the gauge is reset to 0.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page9 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
At the bottom of the Basic Info Window, you will see two different experience gauge bars. The top bar is for your current Base Level, and the bottom one displays experience for your current Job Level.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page10 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
When the Job Level
Experience bar is filled, you will earn a Job Level, and a ^3355FFSkill Point^000000. Skill Points are spent to learn skills for your character.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page11 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
On the right side
of the Basic Info window,
you will see various
Menu buttons.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page12 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Now, one of the most important interfaces is the ^3355FFMini-Map^000000, located at the upper-right of your screen.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page13 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
The minimap is at the upper right. Your position is red; blue dots mark connected warp points. Walk up to a warp to travel to the next area.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page14 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Well, that was my brief overview on in-game interfaces. It might seem like a lot of information now, but it will soon become second nature.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page15 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Let me give you a little bit of Job experience points. Open your Skill Window and distribute your Skill Points into ^3355FFBasic Skills^000000.
>
PAGE npc7554 branch0 page16 mode3 choices0 text<[Kris]
Now, why don't you speak to Edwin? He will teach you more regarding the basic use of Skills. Ah, and let me give you a small present: a Tattered Novice Ninja Suit!
>
PAGE npc7554 branch1 page0 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Hello, may I see your
proof of registration?
>
PAGE npc7554 branch1 page1 mode2 choices0 text<[Kris]
Okay, now
you're ready to go.
