PAGE npc7560 branch0 page0 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Welcome~
Oh look at this
cute little Novice~!
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page1 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
I, Leo Handerson,
feel so responsible for your performance and will be teaching you to the best of my ability. Now, please select the subject you wish to learn.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page2 mode5 choices3 text<>
 CHOICE 0 ordinal1 <Passive and Active skills>
 CHOICE 1 ordinal2 <Basic Skills>
 CHOICE 2 ordinal4 <Cancel.>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page3 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
In Skills, highlight a skill and press X to spend a skill point. Y shows its effects and requirements. Assign an active skill with A, choose a hotbar slot, then confirm with A. Passive skills need no hotbar slot.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page4 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Now, you know that whenever
your Job Level goes up, you earn
a ^3355FFSkill Point^000000, right? Skill Points are used to learn your skills~
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page5 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Basic Skill is passive and has nine ranks. Select it in Skills and press X to learn a rank. Press Y for details. Learn rank 9 before changing to your first job.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page6 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
You'll see to the word 'Passive'
to the right of the Basic Skill icon. That means this skill is Passive, and doesn't use any SP.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page7 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Active Skills, unlike Passive Skills which don't use any SP, require SP each time that
they are used.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page8 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Assign an active skill from Skills or a consumable from Items with A, choose a hotbar slot and confirm with A. In play, LEFT/RIGHT selects an action and UP/DOWN changes bars. Press A to use it.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page9 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
The amount of SP required
to use an Active Skill will be displayed to the right of that skill's icon.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page10 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
Generally, Passive Skills are skills related to mental or physical training and conditioning. The use of special abilities or attacks are Active Skills.
>
PAGE npc7560 branch0 page11 mode2 choices0 text<[Leo Handerson]
If you're still not
sure about my lesson,
I'm willing to go over
it once again.
>
